{"schema_version":"1.0","language":"en","edition":"en-ak","revision":"0","book":{"position":22,"code":"SNG","name":"Song of Songs","testament":"OT"},"chapter":5,"content":[{"type":"para","marker":"p","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"1","sid":"SNG 5:1"},"I am come into my garden, my sister, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["my"]}," spouse: I have gathered my myrrh with my spice; I have eaten my honeycomb with my honey; I have drunk my wine with my milk: eat, O friends; drink, yea, drink abundantly, O beloved. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 5:1"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"p","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"2","sid":"SNG 5:2"},"I sleep, but my heart waketh: ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["it is"]}," the voice of my beloved that knocketh, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["saying,"]}," Open to me, my sister, my love, my dove, my undefiled: for my head is filled with dew, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["and"]}," my locks with the drops of the night. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 5:2"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"3","sid":"SNG 5:3"},"I have put off my coat; how shall I put it on? I have washed my feet; how shall I defile them? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 5:3"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"4","sid":"SNG 5:4"},"My beloved put in his hand by the hole ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["of the door,"]}," and my bowels were moved for him. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 5:4"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"5","sid":"SNG 5:5"},"I rose up to open to my beloved; and my hands dropped ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["with "]},"myrrh, and my fingers ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["with"]}," sweet smelling myrrh, upon the handles of the lock. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 5:5"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"6","sid":"SNG 5:6"},"I opened to my beloved; but my beloved had withdrawn himself, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["and "]},"was gone: my soul failed when he spake: I sought him, but I could not find him; I called him, but he gave me no answer. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 5:6"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"7","sid":"SNG 5:7"},"The watchmen that went about the city found me, they smote me, they wounded me; the keepers of the walls took away my veil from me. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 5:7"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"8","sid":"SNG 5:8"},"I charge you, O daughters of Jerusalem, if ye find my beloved, that ye tell him, that I ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["am"]}," sick of love. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 5:8"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"p","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"9","sid":"SNG 5:9"},"What ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," thy beloved more than ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["another"]}," beloved, O thou fairest among women? what ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," thy beloved more than ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["another "]},"beloved, that thou dost so charge us? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 5:9"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"10","sid":"SNG 5:10"},"My beloved ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," white and ruddy, the chiefest among ten thousand. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 5:10"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"11","sid":"SNG 5:11"},"His head ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is as"]}," the most fine gold, his locks ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["are "]},"bushy, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["and"]}," black as a raven. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 5:11"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"12","sid":"SNG 5:12"},"His eyes ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["are"]}," as ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["the eyes"]}," of doves by the rivers of waters, washed with milk, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["and"]}," fitly set. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 5:12"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"13","sid":"SNG 5:13"},"His cheeks ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["are"]}," as a bed of spices, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["as"]}," sweet flowers: his lips ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["like"]}," lilies, dropping sweet smelling myrrh. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 5:13"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"14","sid":"SNG 5:14"},"His hands ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["are as"]}," gold rings set with the beryl: his belly ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is as"]}," bright ivory overlaid ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["with"]}," sapphires. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 5:14"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"15","sid":"SNG 5:15"},"His legs ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["are as"]}," pillars of marble, set upon sockets of fine gold: his countenance ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," as Lebanon, excellent as the cedars. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 5:15"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"16","sid":"SNG 5:16"},"His mouth ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," most sweet: yea, he ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," altogether lovely. This ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," my beloved, and this ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," my friend, O daughters of Jerusalem. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"SNG 5:16"}]}]}
